{
  "title": "Mailchimp Open Commerce (formerly Reaction Commerce) \u2014 e-commerce / marketplace (12,409\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Mailchimp Open Commerce (formerly Reaction Commerce)\nDomain: e-commerce / marketplace | Scale: large | Stars: 12,409\nProblem: Provides an API-first, headless e-commerce platform that allows retailers to build flexible, scalable online stores without being locked into monolithic solutions. Enables businesses to manage products, inventory, orders, and multi-tenant shops with high performance and composable integrations.\nTarget users: E-commerce businesses, Marketplace operators, API-first development teams, Enterprise retailers, SaaS platform providers\nCore features: Headless GraphQL API; Product management with options and variants; Multi-tenant shop hosting; Inventory and order tracking system; Plugin-based architecture for extensibility; Shipping and tax rate integration; Admin dashboard and order management UI; Customizable email templates\nIntegrations: Mailchimp, Shipping rate providers, Tax rate providers, Custom fulfillment systems, Email service providers\nTech stack: React + Node.js + MongoDB + Docker, Kubernetes\nKey libraries: GraphQL, Express, Babel, ESLint, pnpm, Docker Compose\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure (pnpm workspaces) enables code sharing across API, Admin, and Storefront applications while maintaining independent deployment\n- Plugin system design allows extensibility without modifying core codebase\u2014custom plugins loaded at runtime for shipping, tax, fulfillment, and integrations\n- GraphQL-first API design decouples frontend from backend, enabling headless commerce across multiple storefronts and channels\n- Multi-tenant architecture built into platform core demonstrates enterprise-scale design for hosting multiple shops on shared infrastructure",
